      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Both Bernoulli's principle and Newton's third law are essential and work together in harmony. Bernoulli's principle creates a pressure difference between the upper and lower surfaces of the wing, causing the air molecules to flow faster upwards on the top surface and slower downwards on the bottom surface. This pressure difference creates the lift force. Meanwhile, Newton's third law ensures that as the air 'pushes' the wing downward, the wing simultaneously 'pushes' the air upward with equal force, resulting in an upward net force and lift.",
